<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Delta-K</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose Delta-K, a training-free method to resolve concept omission in Unet and DiT models by directly intervening in the cross-attention mechanism. The core idea is to compute a differential key vector, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K</annotation></semantics></math>, which isolates the semantic information of missing concepts identified from the text by a VLM. At each inference step, we inject <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K</annotation></semantics></math> into the input of the to_k module according to a dynamic strength schedule, forcing the model to attend to these previously neglected concepts during image generation.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Identifying Missing Concepts.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a text prompt <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, we first generate an image <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> through a standard diffusion process. We then employ a Vision-Language Model <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{vlm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{vlm}</annotation></semantics></math> to return two sets of concepts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C_{\text{present}},C_{\text{missing}})=\mathcal{F}_{vlm}(P,I_{base})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>missing</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C_{\text{present}},C_{\text{missing}})=\mathcal{F}_{vlm}(P,I_{base})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of concepts successfully generated in the image, while <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{missing}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>missing</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{missing}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of incorrectly generated or missing concepts, which are the targets for our subsequent enhancement.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Delta-K augmentation.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we construct the masked prompt <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{missing}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>missing</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{missing}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span>, and capture the inputs to the <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">to_k</span> module for both <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the original prompt <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> during inference to obtain <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{input}}(P_{\text{mask}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{input}}(P_{\text{mask}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{input}}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{input}}(P)</annotation></semantics></math>. Their difference <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K</annotation></semantics></math> illustrates the semantic representation of the missing concepts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K\triangleq K_{\text{input}}(P)-K_{\text{input}}(P_{\text{mask}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K\triangleq K_{\text{input}}(P)-K_{\text{input}}(P_{\text{mask}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During the inferencing, for each layer and step <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we inject this pre-computed <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta K</annotation></semantics></math> into the current step’s key vector and compute the attention as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K^{\prime}=K+\alpha_{t}\cdot\Delta K,\quad\mathrm{Attn}{{}^{\prime}}=\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q\cdot{K^{\prime}}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>Attn</mi><mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></mmultiscripts><mi>Softmax</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>K</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}=K+\alpha_{t}\cdot\Delta K,\quad\mathrm{Attn}{{}^{\prime}}=\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q\cdot{K^{\prime}}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The augmentation strength is controlled by a dynamic scheduling function <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. By directly augmenting the key vectors, our method boosts the attention weights of missing concepts to ensure their generation in the final image.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Dynamic scheduling</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Motivated by these observations, we introduce a dynamic scheduling method that adaptively adjusts the augmentation strength <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at each denoising step <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective is to guide the attention received by the missing concepts <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{missing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{missing}</annotation></semantics></math> to match the attention pattern of successfully generated concepts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> the average attention received by the successfully generated concepts <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math> in baseline generation. At denoising step <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and layer <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, given the baseline attention map <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t,l)}_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>base</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t,l)}_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the token index set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{present}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{present}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the target attention is computed as</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t,l)}_{\text{target}}(\alpha_{t})=\frac{1}{|I_{\text{present}}|}\sum_{i\in I_{\text{present}}}A^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})_{\text{base},i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>present</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>base</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t,l)}_{\text{target}}(\alpha_{t})=\frac{1}{|I_{\text{present}}|}\sum_{i\in I_{\text{present}}}A^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})_{\text{base},i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the target attention distribution <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{target}^{(t,l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{target}^{(t,l)}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from the baseline generation, representing the attention pattern of successfully generated concepts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To encourage the attention distribution of missing concepts to match the target distribution, we minimize the following objective:</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})=\left\|{A_{\text{missing}}^{\prime}}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})-A_{\text{target}}^{(t,l)}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mtext>missing</mtext><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})=\left\|{A_{\text{missing}}^{\prime}}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})-A_{\text{target}}^{(t,l)}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This objective encourages the model to gradually align the attention allocation of missing concepts with that of successful ones.
Since the loss function is differentiable with respect to the augmentation strength <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we perform an online optimization at each denoising step <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal coefficient is obtained by minimizing the aggregated gradient magnitude across layers:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{*}=\lambda\cdot\arg\min_{\alpha_{t}}\left\|\sum_{l}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})}{\partial\alpha_{t}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>l</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{*}=\lambda\cdot\arg\min_{\alpha_{t}}\left\|\sum_{l}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t})}{\partial\alpha_{t}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, we solve this optimization using the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2014</a>]</cite>. This dynamic optimization allows the augmentation strength to adapt to the generation process, stabilizing the attention signal of missing concepts and transforming noisy attention patterns into coherent semantic representations. We augment the key and compute cross-attention in a standard form:</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attn}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t}^{*})=\mathrm{Softmax}\!\left(\frac{Q^{(t,l)}\left(K^{(t,l)}+\alpha_{t}^{*}\Delta K^{(t,l)}\right)^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V^{(t,l)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.922em;" width="3.922em"><mi>Softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attn}^{(t,l)}(\alpha_{t}^{*})=\mathrm{Softmax}\!\left(\frac{Q^{(t,l)}\left(K^{(t,l)}+\alpha_{t}^{*}\Delta K^{(t,l)}\right)^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)V^{(t,l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The overall Delta-K algorithm can be summarized as shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Spatial Instability: Representation vs. Activation. ‣ 3.2 Dynamics of Failure ‣ 3 Motivation: Concept Omission in Latent Space ‣ Delta-K: Boosting Multi-Instance Generation via Cross-Attention Augmentation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Experiments on Geneval. Higher is better (<math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:56.7pt;vertical-align:-27.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-162.3pt,26.7pt) scale(0.515308922752572,0.515308922752572) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Model</span></th>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Overall<math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Single</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Two</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Counting</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Colors</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Position</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Color</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">object</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">object</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">attribution</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Seedream 3.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>]</cite></th>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.99</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.96</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.91</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.93</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.47</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.80</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.84</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="8"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Earlier Generative Models</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">minDALL-E <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dayma et al., 2021</a>]</cite></th>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.23</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.73</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.11</td>
